    <section class="chapter wide needs-partners" id="ch-nickel-test">
      <span class="eyebrow">10 · The test</span>
      <h2>The nickel question this case never asked</h2>
      <p>Chapter 03 showed processed-nickel exports growing roughly fifteen-fold while ore
      exports went to zero. That is an export-side fact. It implies an import-side one: you
      cannot build dozens of smelters without buying the furnaces, the electrodes and the
      inputs to feed them. If the story is true, it should be visible in what Indonesia
      <em>bought</em>.</p>
      <p>So we pre-registered the test before looking, and committed the thresholds to the
      repository before computing a single import number. Base window 2013–2015, peak window
      2021–2024. <b>H1</b>: imports of machinery and electrical equipment (HS 84 + 85) rise at
      least 50%. <b>H2</b>: that rise beats total import growth by at least 10 points, so a
      general import boom cannot pass on its own. <b>H3</b>: at least one smelter input —
      coke, graphite electrodes, chrome ore, stainless scrap — at least doubles. All three is
      a pass; two is partial; fewer is a failure, and it publishes as one.</p>
      <div id="gate-b7" class="gate-card"></div>
      <p class="big-stat">It failed. Capital-goods imports grew
      <b class="copper">{growthPct(pm?.nickel?.capGrowth)}</b> while <em>all</em> imports grew
      <b class="copper">{growthPct(pm?.nickel?.totalGrowth)}</b> — the smelter build-out is
      essentially invisible in the machinery bill.</p>
      <p>That is a real result and it stands. Indonesia’s furnace purchases are either too
      small against a {bn(pm?.totalImp)} import bill to register, spread across too many years
      to show up in a window comparison, or booked as investment flows the goods data never
      sees. On the capital-goods hypothesis, the answer is no.</p>
      <p>But look at what the test found on its way to failing. The feedstock did not grow —
      it detonated. {bigInput ? `${bigInput.label} imports rose ` : ""}
      <b class="copper">{bigInput ? timesX(bigInput.growth) : "—"}</b>
      {bigInput ? "between the same two windows" : ""}, and imported coal — in the country
      that exports more coal than any other on earth — rose
      <b class="copper">{rv ? timesX(rv.inputs.rows.find((r) => r.code === "2701").growth) : "—"}</b>
      to {rv ? bn(rv.inputs.rows.find((r) => r.code === "2701").peak) : "—"} a year. Coke,
      quicklime and limestone flux all more than tripled. Ferrous scrap, which we expected to
      rise, fell.</p>
      <p>So the smelters are visible in the import data after all; we simply pointed the
      instrument at the wrong shelf. Downstreaming did not show up as a one-off equipment
      purchase. It showed up as a <em>permanent new import dependency</em> —
      <b>{rv ? bn(rv.inputs.added) : "—"} a year</b> of coal, coke, chrome and flux that Indonesia
      did not previously buy, set against <b>{rv ? bn(rv.nickel.gain) : "—"} a year</b> of
      <em>additional</em> processed-nickel exports.
      <b>{rv ? (rv.inputs.shareOfGain * 100).toFixed(1) : "—"}%</b> of the headline gain is spent
      buying the inputs that make it possible — and this bill scales with the
      {x1(nk?.tonnes)} rise in tonnage from chapter 03, not with the {x1(nk?.value)} rise in
      receipts. Two things it does not count: the {rv ? bn(rv.nickel.oreForegone) : "—"} a year of
      ore exports given up, and the domestic coal burned in the smelters' captive power plants,
      which never appears in an import statistic. The figure is a floor.</p>
      <p class="footnote"><b>Corrected after review.</b> This paragraph previously set the input
      bill against "US$28.5B a year of additional processed-nickel exports" and called the ratio
      "around an eighth". {rv ? bn(rv.nickel.vPeak) : "—"} is the peak-window <em>level</em>; the
      increment over the base window is {rv ? bn(rv.nickel.gain) : "—"}, which makes the ratio
      nearer a seventh. The direction of the argument is unchanged; the arithmetic was wrong and
      is now computed rather than typed.</p>
      <div id="nickel-test" class="chart"></div>
      <div class="sub-head"><span class="eyebrow">The input basket</span>
        <span class="stamp dim">BASE 2013–15 → PEAK 2021–24 · THRESHOLD +100%</span></div>
      <div id="nickel-inputs" class="spark-grid"></div>
      <p class="footnote"><b>A prior we got wrong, on the record.</b> Coal and limestone were
      entered as <em>controls</em> — Indonesia has both domestically, so we predicted they
      would not move. They moved the most. The likely reason is geographic and metallurgical
      rather than statistical: the smelters sit in Sulawesi, far from the Kalimantan and
      Sumatra coal basins, and much Indonesian coal is thermal grade rather than the
      metallurgical input a furnace wants. That explanation is an inference, not a
      measurement, and is flagged as such.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter needs-partners" id="ch-recon">
      <span class="eyebrow">Reconciliation</span>
      <h2>No, and that is worth saying out loud</h2>
      <p>Two totals, two published benchmarks, tolerances fixed before either was computed.
      The import side reconciles almost exactly. The export side does not: BACI puts
      Indonesia’s goods exports roughly a sixth above what Indonesia itself reports, every
      year we can check. <b>The export-reconciliation check fails</b>, and rather than quietly widening the tolerance we
      are printing the gap.</p>
      <div id="recon" class="gate-card"></div>
      <p>The gap is not an artefact of this extension. It is systematic across years, it is
      spread across chapters rather than sitting in one product, and it is not caused by
      aggregate or “nes” partner codes — every destination in the file is a real economy. The
      leading explanation is that BACI is a <em>mirror-reconciled reconstruction</em>: it
      harmonises what Indonesia says it shipped against what its 213 partners say they
      received, and for Indonesia the partners consistently report receiving more. That gap
      is a well-documented feature of Indonesian commodity trade, not a bug in this pipeline
      — and our totals reproduce the case’s existing export figures to nine significant
      figures, so the discrepancy is between BACI and Jakarta, not between us and BACI.</p>
      <p class="footnote"><b>Does this undermine chapters 01–06?</b> Largely no, and for a
      structural reason: economic complexity is computed from revealed comparative advantage,
      which is a ratio of <em>shares</em>. A level difference that is roughly proportional
      across products cancels in the numerator and denominator. It does matter for any
      statement about levels — which is why the hero quotes UN Comtrade’s US$259.5B for 2023
      and not BACI’s figure, and why every dollar total in chapters 07–10 is labelled as
      BACI’s.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter review-cta">
      <span class="eyebrow">Review</span>
      <h2>Audited adversarially, by its own author.</h2>
      <p>A second read of the same data against the published literature, written to attack the first. It was done by the person who built the instrument — no external reviewer has checked it, and one person reviews everything here — if you would like to be the first, breaking a gate here is worth more than another instrument. It runs the rank
      correlation against the Harvard Atlas that this repository registered and never computed —
      it passes at ρ {gb1 ? gb1.mean.toFixed(3) : "—"} — and then shows why the rank this page
      leads with still cannot bear the weight: {dens?.neighbours?.length ?? "—"} economies sit
      inside {dens ? Math.round(dens.tenPlacesInSd * 100) : "—"}% of one standard deviation of
      Indonesia. It reads the tonnes the case never opened, and finds {x1(nk?.tonnes)} the
      material for {x1(nk?.value)} the money. And it corrects three claims this page used to
      make — about the neighbours' decade, about the supplier side, and about the arithmetic of
      the nickel gain.</p>
      <a class="cta big" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "")}/article`}>Read the review article →</a>
    </section>

    <footer class="method">
      <span class="eyebrow">Methodology &amp; sources</span>
      <p>Flows: CEPII BACI release 202601 (HS92, 1995–{latest}, Etalab 2.0 licence), ~330M
      rows in DuckDB. Sample: economies with population ≥ 1M (World Bank) and total trade
      ≥ US$1B per year — the Atlas rules. Complexity: Balassa RCA → M matrix (RCA ≥ 1) →
      ECI/PCI via Harvard Growth Lab’s <code>py-ecomplexity</code> at HS4, PCI sign normalized
      to Atlas convention (no year required flipping). Product space: maximum-spanning-tree
      backbone + proximity ≥ 0.55, seeded 3-D force layout computed once; the “altitude”
      view replaces layout depth with PCI. Product search is lexical over every HS6
      description (prefix and one-edit fuzzy matching) plus semantic: each product’s
      descriptions are embedded with a locally hosted multilingual-E5 model served by the
      lab’s own embedding endpoint, so a query in Bahasa Indonesia finds English product
      names — the same local-embedding capability that powers Provenance. (A fully static
      alternative would run the encoder in-browser with transformers.js, at the cost of a
      30–100 MB first-visit download.) <b>Caveats stated plainly:</b> goods only; the
      log-supermodularity condition — Growth Lab’s structural-ranking check — holds for
      roughly a third of country-product pairs in early years, so ECI is a ranking, not a
      cardinal measure — see chapter 04 for how little ten places of it separate.
      <b>Rank check:</b> the registered test is a rank correlation against the Harvard Atlas's
      published HS92 complexity index in every overlapping year, threshold ρ ≥
      {gb1 ? gb1.threshold.toFixed(2) : "—"}. Computed during the review, it returns
      {gb1 ? gb1.min.toFixed(3) : "—"}–{gb1 ? gb1.max.toFixed(3) : "—"} (mean
      {gb1 ? gb1.mean.toFixed(3) : "—"}) over {rv?.nYears ?? 30} years and
      <b>passes in every one</b>. On Indonesia's own seat the pipelines differ by more: ranked
      over the Atlas's own country list, #{at?.latest?.onAtlasSample ?? "—"} here against
      #{at?.latest?.atlas ?? "—"} there in {latest}. An earlier version of this page compared our
      {rv?.rank?.validationYear ?? 2023} rank to an Atlas figure that is the Atlas's {latest} one,
      and reported agreement "within three places"; that comparison was withdrawn.</p>
      <p><b>Why chapters 01–06 use exports only.</b> Not an omission: economic complexity is
      defined through revealed comparative advantage, which compares a country’s share of
      world exports of a product against that product’s share of world exports. Imports have
      no place in that ratio — an “import ECI” would rank countries by what they can afford,
      not by what they can make. Chapters 07–10 add the import and partner sides as their own
      analysis rather than folding them into the complexity math.</p>
      <p><b>Partners &amp; imports (07–10).</b> Same BACI release, streamed year by year and
      filtered to flows where Indonesia is exporter or importer; the 330M-row corpus is never
      rebuilt for this. Values are FOB in both directions — BACI strips CIF margins out of
      importer declarations, which is why our import total sits a few per cent below the BPS
      headline (see the reconciliation card). Partners are BACI reporting territories:
      <b>Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan (“Other Asia, nes”) are counted separately from
      China</b>; folding them in would raise the reported China share. Concentration is the
      Herfindahl–Hirschman index over partner shares, alongside the top-five share.
      <b>The three partner-and-import checks</b> were given numeric thresholds in <code>pipeline/config.py</code>
      before any partner or import number was computed, and failures publish red above rather
      than being quietly dropped.</p>
      <span class="stamp dim">AN OPENSTUDY.ID INSTRUMENT · ANNUAL REBUILD · {exportsB ? `IDN GOODS EXPORTS ${latest}: US$${exportsB}B` : ""}</span>
    </footer>
    <div id="chart-tip" hidden></div>

    <script>
      import * as d3 from "d3";
      import * as THREE from "three";
      import { OrbitControls } from "three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js";

      /* visible failure beats silent emptiness: any uncaught error paints a banner */
      const failBanner = (msg) => {
        let b = document.getElementById("err-banner");
        if (!b) {
          b = document.createElement("div"); b.id = "err-banner";
          b.style.cssText = "position:fixed;bottom:0;left:0;right:0;z-index:99;background:#3A1E1A;color:#F26D5B;font:12px ui-monospace,monospace;padding:10px 16px;border-top:1px solid #F26D5B;";
          document.body.appendChild(b);
        }
        b.textContent = "⚠ " + msg;
      };
      addEventListener("error", (e) => failBanner("Script error: " + (e.message ?? e.type)));
      addEventListener("unhandledrejection", (e) => failBanner("Load error: " + (e.reason?.message ?? e.reason)));
      /* run each section independently — one failure must not blank the page */
      const sect = (name, fn) => { try { return fn(); } catch (err) { console.error(name, err); failBanner(`${name} failed: ${err.message ?? err}`); return null; } };

      const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
      const COPPER = "#D9722C", SILVER = "#AEB6C2", VERDIGRIS = "#58A89B", INK = "#0C0F14";
      const SECTORS = [ // [maxHS2, label, color] — desaturated for the dark ground
        [5, "Animal", "#8C7A6B"], [15, "Vegetable & fats", "#7E9A6C"], [24, "Foodstuffs", "#A48E5A"],
        [27, "Minerals & fuels", "#6E7887"], [38, "Chemicals", "#7D6F9C"], [40, "Plastics & rubber", "#6C8FA1"],
        [43, "Hides", "#8D7355"], [49, "Wood & paper", "#7C8A61"], [63, "Textiles", "#9A6F86"],
        [67, "Footwear", "#8F7D9A"], [71, "Stone, glass, gems", "#6F97A6"], [83, "Metals", "#9AA3AF"],
        [85, "Machinery & electrical", "#5D8FBF"], [89, "Transport", "#5FA8B5"], [99, "Instruments & misc", "#B0A46B"],
      ];
      const sectorOf = (hs2) => SECTORS.find(([max]) => +hs2 <= max);
      const reduced = matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches;
      const load = (f) => fetch(`${base}/data/${f}`).then((r) => { if (!r.ok) throw f; return r.json(); });

      let space, names, states, treemap, traj, nickel, adjacency;
      try {
        [space, names, states, treemap, traj, nickel, adjacency] = await Promise.all(
          ["product_space.json", "names.json", "space_states.json", "treemap.json",
           "trajectory.json", "nickel.json", "adjacency.json"].map(load));
      } catch (missing) {
        document.getElementById("hero-status").textContent =
          `PIPELINE STILL RUNNING — ${missing} not yet exported. Refresh in a few minutes.`;
        throw missing;
      }
      const latest = String(space.year);
      const label = (id) => names[id] ?? `HS ${id}`;

      /* shared chart tooltip + end-label de-collision */
      const ctip = document.getElementById("chart-tip");
      const showTip = (e, html) => { ctip.hidden = false; ctip.innerHTML = html; ctip.style.left = e.pageX + 14 + "px"; ctip.style.top = e.pageY + 14 + "px"; };
      const hideTip = () => { ctip.hidden = true; };
      const fmt$ = (v) => "$" + d3.format(".3s")(v).replace("G", "B");
      function spread(items, minGap, lo, hi) {
        items.sort((a, b) => a.y - b.y);
        for (let i = 1; i < items.length; i++) if (items[i].y - items[i - 1].y < minGap) items[i].y = items[i - 1].y + minGap;
        const over = items.at(-1).y - hi;
        if (over > 0) for (const it of items) it.y -= over;
        for (let i = items.length - 2; i >= 0; i--) if (items[i + 1].y - items[i].y < minGap) items[i].y = items[i + 1].y - minGap;
        if (items[0].y < lo) { const up = lo - items[0].y; for (const it of items) it.y += up; }
        return items;
      }

      /* ---------- 3-D product space (shared by hero + explore) ---------- */
      const SPAN = 120;
      const ext = (k) => d3.extent(space.nodes, (n) => n[k] ?? 0);
      const sx = d3.scaleLinear(ext("x"), [-SPAN, SPAN]);
      const sy = d3.scaleLinear(ext("y"), [-SPAN, SPAN]);
      const sz = d3.scaleLinear(ext("z"), [-SPAN, SPAN]);
      const spci = d3.scaleLinear(ext("pci"), [-SPAN * 0.7, SPAN * 0.7]);
      const rScale = d3.scaleSqrt(d3.extent(space.nodes, (n) => n.trade), [2.2, 11]);
      // hero reveal order: by sector, then trade — nodes stream in sector by sector
      const order = [...space.nodes].sort((a, b) =>
        sectorOf(a.hs2)[1].localeCompare(sectorOf(b.hs2)[1]) || a.trade - b.trade);
      const indexOf = new Map(order.map((n, i) => [n.id, i]));

      const POINT_VS = `
        attribute float size; attribute vec3 color; attribute float alpha;
        varying vec3 vColor; varying float vAlpha;
        void main() {
          vColor = color; vAlpha = alpha;
          vec4 mv = modelViewMatrix * vec4(position, 1.0);
          gl_PointSize = size * (420.0 / -mv.z);
          gl_Position = projectionMatrix * mv;
        }`;
      const POINT_FS = `
        varying vec3 vColor; varying float vAlpha;
        void main() {
          float d = length(gl_PointCoord - 0.5);
          if (d > 0.5) discard;
          float edge = smoothstep(0.5, 0.36, d);
          gl_FragColor = vec4(vColor, vAlpha * edge);
        }`;

      function makeSpace(canvas, { interactive }) {
        const renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ canvas, antialias: true, alpha: false });
        renderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(devicePixelRatio, 2));
        renderer.setClearColor(new THREE.Color(INK), 1);
        const scene = new THREE.Scene();
        scene.fog = new THREE.Fog(new THREE.Color(INK), SPAN * 1.6, SPAN * 5);
        const camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(48, 1, 1, 4000);
        camera.position.set(0, SPAN * 0.35, SPAN * 2.6);
        const controls = new OrbitControls(camera, canvas);
        controls.enableDamping = true; controls.dampingFactor = 0.06;
        controls.enablePan = false; controls.minDistance = SPAN * 0.6; controls.maxDistance = SPAN * 5;
        controls.autoRotate = !reduced; controls.autoRotateSpeed = interactive ? 0.25 : 0.55;
        controls.enabled = interactive;

        const n = order.length;
        const pos = new Float32Array(n * 3), col = new Float32Array(n * 3);
        const size = new Float32Array(n), alpha = new Float32Array(n);
        const geo = new THREE.BufferGeometry();
        geo.setAttribute("position", new THREE.BufferAttribute(pos, 3));
        geo.setAttribute("color", new THREE.BufferAttribute(col, 3));
        geo.setAttribute("size", new THREE.BufferAttribute(size, 1));
        geo.setAttribute("alpha", new THREE.BufferAttribute(alpha, 1));
        const pts = new THREE.Points(geo, new THREE.ShaderMaterial({
          vertexShader: POINT_VS, fragmentShader: POINT_FS, transparent: true, depthWrite: false }));
        scene.add(pts);
        // copper glow layer: same positions, only lit nodes visible, additive
        const gsize = new Float32Array(n), galpha = new Float32Array(n), gcol = new Float32Array(n * 3);
        const ggeo = new THREE.BufferGeometry();
        ggeo.setAttribute("position", new THREE.BufferAttribute(pos, 3));
        ggeo.setAttribute("color", new THREE.BufferAttribute(gcol, 3));
        ggeo.setAttribute("size", new THREE.BufferAttribute(gsize, 1));
        ggeo.setAttribute("alpha", new THREE.BufferAttribute(galpha, 1));
        const glow = new THREE.Points(ggeo, new THREE.ShaderMaterial({
          vertexShader: POINT_VS, fragmentShader: POINT_FS, transparent: true, depthWrite: false,
          blending: THREE.AdditiveBlending }));
        scene.add(glow);
        // edges
        const idIndex = new Map(space.nodes.map((nd) => [nd.id, nd]));
        const epos = new Float32Array(space.edges.length * 6);
        const egeo = new THREE.BufferGeometry();
        egeo.setAttribute("position", new THREE.BufferAttribute(epos, 3));
        const edges = new THREE.LineSegments(egeo, new THREE.LineBasicMaterial({
          color: new THREE.Color(SILVER), transparent: true, opacity: 0.16, depthWrite: false }));
        scene.add(edges);
        // hover ring
        const ring = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.RingGeometry(1, 1.25, 40),
          new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: "#E6E8EC", side: THREE.DoubleSide, transparent: true, opacity: 0.9 }));
        ring.visible = false; scene.add(ring);

        let mode = "net", lit = new Set(states[latest] ?? []), filter = null, progress = 1;
        const copper = new THREE.Color(COPPER);
        const zOf = (nd) => mode === "pci" ? spci(nd.pci) : sz(nd.z ?? 0);

        function layoutPositions() {
          order.forEach((nd, i) => { pos[i * 3] = sx(nd.x); pos[i * 3 + 1] = zOf(nd); pos[i * 3 + 2] = sy(nd.y); });
          geo.attributes.position.needsUpdate = true; ggeo.attributes.position.needsUpdate = true;
          space.edges.forEach(([a, b], k) => {
            const na = idIndex.get(a), nb = idIndex.get(b);
            if (!na || !nb) return;
            epos.set([sx(na.x), zOf(na), sy(na.y), sx(nb.x), zOf(nb), sy(nb.y)], k * 6);
          });
          egeo.attributes.position.needsUpdate = true;
          geo.computeBoundingSphere();
        }
        function paint() {
          order.forEach((nd, i) => {
            const isLit = lit.has(nd.id), dim = filter && !filter.has(nd.id);
            const c = isLit ? copper : new THREE.Color(sectorOf(nd.hs2)[2]);
            col.set([c.r, c.g, c.b], i * 3);
            size[i] = rScale(nd.trade) * (isLit ? 1.15 : 1);
            alpha[i] = dim ? 0.08 : isLit ? 0.98 : 0.62;
            gcol.set([copper.r, copper.g, copper.b], i * 3);
            gsize[i] = rScale(nd.trade) * 3.2;
            galpha[i] = isLit && !dim ? 0.22 : 0;
          });
          geo.attributes.color.needsUpdate = geo.attributes.size.needsUpdate = geo.attributes.alpha.needsUpdate = true;
          ggeo.attributes.color.needsUpdate = ggeo.attributes.size.needsUpdate = ggeo.attributes.alpha.needsUpdate = true;
        }
        function reveal() {
          const shown = Math.floor(n * Math.min(progress, 1));
          geo.setDrawRange(0, shown); ggeo.setDrawRange(0, shown);
          edges.material.opacity = progress > 0.7 ? 0.16 * Math.min((progress - 0.7) / 0.3, 1) : 0;
        }
        function size2() {
          const W = canvas.clientWidth, H = canvas.clientHeight;
          renderer.setSize(W, H, false); camera.aspect = W / H; camera.updateProjectionMatrix();
        }
        size2(); addEventListener("resize", size2);
        layoutPositions(); paint(); reveal();

        if (interactive) {
          const tip = document.getElementById("ps-tip");
          const ray = new THREE.Raycaster(); ray.params.Points.threshold = 3.2;
          const mouse = new THREE.Vector2();
          let hovered = null;
          canvas.addEventListener("mousemove", (e) => {
            const rect = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
            mouse.set(((e.clientX - rect.left) / rect.width) * 2 - 1, -((e.clientY - rect.top) / rect.height) * 2 + 1);
            ray.setFromCamera(mouse, camera);
            const hit = ray.intersectObject(pts, false).sort((a, b) => a.distanceToRay - b.distanceToRay)[0];
            if (hit && alpha[hit.index] > 0.2) {
              const nd = order[hit.index]; hovered = nd;
              ring.visible = true; ring.position.set(pos[hit.index * 3], pos[hit.index * 3 + 1], pos[hit.index * 3 + 2]);
              ring.scale.setScalar(rScale(nd.trade) * 0.55 + 1.2); ring.lookAt(camera.position);
              tip.hidden = false; tip.style.left = e.clientX - rect.left + 14 + "px"; tip.style.top = e.clientY - rect.top + 14 + "px";
              tip.innerHTML = `<b>${label(nd.id)}</b><br>HS ${nd.id} · ${sectorOf(nd.hs2)[1]}<br>PCI ${nd.pci.toFixed(2)} · world trade $${d3.format(".3s")(nd.trade * 1e3)}<br>${lit.has(nd.id) ? "<span class='copper'>● Indonesia exports competitively</span>" : "<span class='dim'>○ not yet an Indonesian strength</span>"}`;
            } else { hovered = null; ring.visible = false; tip.hidden = true; }
          });
          canvas.addEventListener("mouseleave", () => { ring.visible = false; tip.hidden = true; });
          canvas.addEventListener("pointerdown", () => { controls.autoRotate = false; });
        }

        let running = true;
        const io = new IntersectionObserver(([en]) => { running = en.isIntersecting; }, { threshold: 0.05 });
        io.observe(canvas);
        function frame() {
          requestAnimationFrame(frame);
          if (!running) return;
          controls.update();
          if (ring.visible) ring.lookAt(camera.position);
          renderer.render(scene, camera);
        }
        frame();

        return {
          setYear(yr) { lit = new Set(states[String(yr)] ?? []); paint(); },
          setFilter(ids) { filter = ids && ids.size ? ids : null; paint(); },
          setMode(m) { mode = m; layoutPositions(); },
          focus(id) {
            const i = indexOf.get(id); if (i == null) return;
            const p = new THREE.Vector3(pos[i * 3], pos[i * 3 + 1], pos[i * 3 + 2]);
            controls.autoRotate = false;
            const dir = camera.position.clone().sub(controls.target).normalize();
            controls.target.copy(p);
            camera.position.copy(p.clone().add(dir.multiplyScalar(SPAN * 0.9)));
            ring.visible = true; ring.position.copy(p); ring.scale.setScalar(rScale(order[i].trade) * 0.55 + 1.2);
          },
          animate(ms) {
            if (reduced) { progress = 1; reveal(); return; }
            progress = 0; reveal();
            const t0 = performance.now();
            const step = (t) => {
              progress = Math.min((t - t0) / ms, 1); reveal();
              if (progress < 1) requestAnimationFrame(step);
              else document.getElementById("hero-status").textContent =
                `${space.nodes.length} PRODUCTS · ${space.edges.length} LINKS · ${lit.size} INDONESIAN STRENGTHS IN ${latest} · 3-D FORCE LAYOUT`;
            };
            requestAnimationFrame(step);
          },
        };
      }
      /* ---------- canvas fallback: software 3-D, no WebGL required ----------
         Same layout and the same interactions as the WebGL scene — auto-rotate,
         drag to orbit, wheel to zoom, depth fog, copper glow, hover, PCI altitude —
         projected by hand onto a 2-D canvas (~1.2k points, ~2k edges: cheap). */
      function makeSpace2D(canvas, { interactive }) {
        const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");
        const dpr = Math.min(devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);
        const n = order.length;
        const edgeIdx = space.edges.map(([a, b]) => [indexOf.get(a), indexOf.get(b)]).filter(([a, b]) => a != null && b != null);
        const P = new Float32Array(n * 3);     // world positions (x, altitude, y) — as in makeSpace
        const SX = new Float32Array(n), SY = new Float32Array(n), SD = new Float32Array(n); // screen x, y, depth
        const byDepth = Array.from({ length: n }, (_, i) => i);
        let W, H, mode = "net", lit = new Set(states[latest] ?? []), filter = null, progress = 1, hovered = -1;
        // orbit state mirrors the OrbitControls setup above (camera at (0, .35, 2.6)·SPAN)
        const cam = { yaw: 0, pitch: Math.atan2(0.35, 2.6), dist: SPAN * Math.hypot(0.35, 2.6), target: [0, 0, 0] };
        const MIN_D = SPAN * 0.6, MAX_D = SPAN * 5, FOG_NEAR = SPAN * 1.6, FOG_FAR = SPAN * 5;
        const autoSpeed = interactive ? 0.026 : 0.057;   // rad/s ≈ OrbitControls autoRotateSpeed 0.25 / 0.55
        let auto = !reduced, dragging = false, vyaw = 0, vpitch = 0, mouse = null;
        const F = () => (H / 2) / Math.tan((48 / 2) * Math.PI / 180);
        const zOf = (nd) => mode === "pci" ? spci(nd.pci) : sz(nd.z ?? 0);
        const layoutPositions = () => order.forEach((nd, i) => { P[i * 3] = sx(nd.x); P[i * 3 + 1] = zOf(nd); P[i * 3 + 2] = sy(nd.y); });
        function size() {
          W = canvas.clientWidth; H = canvas.clientHeight;
          canvas.width = W * dpr; canvas.height = H * dpr; ctx.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);
        }
        // copper glow sprite — one radial gradient scaled per lit node (shadowBlur per arc is far too slow)
        const sprite = document.createElement("canvas"); sprite.width = sprite.height = 64;
        { const g = sprite.getContext("2d"); const rg = g.createRadialGradient(32, 32, 0, 32, 32, 32);
          rg.addColorStop(0, "rgba(217,114,44,0.60)"); rg.addColorStop(0.35, "rgba(217,114,44,0.20)"); rg.addColorStop(1, "rgba(217,114,44,0)");
          g.fillStyle = rg; g.fillRect(0, 0, 64, 64); }

        function project() {
          const cy = Math.cos(cam.yaw), syw = Math.sin(cam.yaw), cp = Math.cos(cam.pitch), sp = Math.sin(cam.pitch);
          const f = F(), [tx, ty, tz] = cam.target;
          for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            const x = P[i * 3] - tx, y = P[i * 3 + 1] - ty, z = P[i * 3 + 2] - tz;
            const x1 = x * cy - z * syw, z1 = x * syw + z * cy;        // orbit (yaw)
            const y2 = y * cp - z1 * sp, z2 = y * sp + z1 * cp;        // elevation (pitch)
            const depth = cam.dist - z2;                               // camera sits at +dist on the view axis
            SD[i] = depth;
            if (depth < 1) continue;
            SX[i] = W / 2 + (f * x1) / depth; SY[i] = H / 2 - (f * y2) / depth;
          }
          byDepth.sort((a, b) => SD[b] - SD[a]);                       // far → near
        }
        const fog = (d) => Math.max(0, Math.min(1, (FOG_FAR - d) / (FOG_FAR - FOG_NEAR)));
        function draw() {
          project();
          ctx.fillStyle = INK; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);
          const shown = Math.floor(n * Math.min(progress, 1));
          const f = F();
          if (progress > 0.7) {
            ctx.globalAlpha = 0.16 * Math.min((progress - 0.7) / 0.3, 1); ctx.strokeStyle = SILVER; ctx.lineWidth = 0.6;
            ctx.beginPath();
            for (const [a, b] of edgeIdx) {
              if (a >= shown || b >= shown || SD[a] < 1 || SD[b] < 1) continue;
              ctx.moveTo(SX[a], SY[a]); ctx.lineTo(SX[b], SY[b]);
            }
            ctx.stroke();
          }
          for (const i of byDepth) {
            if (i >= shown || SD[i] < 1) continue;
            const nd = order[i], isLit = lit.has(nd.id), dim = filter && !filter.has(nd.id);
            const r = (rScale(nd.trade) * f * 0.62) / SD[i], k = fog(SD[i]);
            if (isLit && !dim) { ctx.globalAlpha = 0.85 * k; const g = r * 7; ctx.drawImage(sprite, SX[i] - g / 2, SY[i] - g / 2, g, g); }
            ctx.globalAlpha = (dim ? 0.08 : isLit ? 0.98 : 0.62) * k;
            ctx.fillStyle = isLit ? COPPER : sectorOf(nd.hs2)[2];
            ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(SX[i], SY[i], r, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();
          }
          if (hovered >= 0 && SD[hovered] >= 1) {
            const r = (rScale(order[hovered].trade) * f * 0.62) / SD[hovered];
            ctx.globalAlpha = 0.9; ctx.strokeStyle = "#E6E8EC"; ctx.lineWidth = 1.3;
            ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(SX[hovered], SY[hovered], r + 4, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.stroke();
          }
          ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
        }
        size(); addEventListener("resize", size);
        layoutPositions();

        if (interactive) {
          const tip = document.getElementById("ps-tip");
          canvas.style.touchAction = "none"; canvas.style.cursor = "grab";
          let last = null;
          canvas.addEventListener("pointerdown", (e) => { auto = false; dragging = true; last = [e.clientX, e.clientY]; vyaw = vpitch = 0; canvas.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId); canvas.style.cursor = "grabbing"; });
          canvas.addEventListener("pointerup", (e) => { dragging = false; canvas.style.cursor = "grab"; try { canvas.releasePointerCapture(e.pointerId); } catch {} });
          canvas.addEventListener("pointercancel", () => { dragging = false; });
          canvas.addEventListener("pointermove", (e) => {
            const rect = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
            mouse = [e.clientX - rect.left, e.clientY - rect.top];
            if (dragging && last) {
              const dx = e.clientX - last[0], dy = e.clientY - last[1]; last = [e.clientX, e.clientY];
              vyaw = -dx * 0.005; vpitch = dy * 0.005;
              cam.yaw += vyaw; cam.pitch = Math.max(-1.35, Math.min(1.35, cam.pitch + vpitch));
            }
          });
          canvas.addEventListener("mouseleave", () => { mouse = null; hovered = -1; tip.hidden = true; });
          canvas.addEventListener("wheel", (e) => { e.preventDefault(); cam.dist = Math.max(MIN_D, Math.min(MAX_D, cam.dist * Math.exp(e.deltaY * 0.0012))); }, { passive: false });
          // hover is resolved every frame (the scene moves under a still pointer)
          var resolveHover = () => {
            if (!mouse || dragging) return;
            const shown = Math.floor(n * Math.min(progress, 1));
            let best = -1, bestD = 12 * 12;
            for (let i = 0; i < shown; i++) {
              if (SD[i] < 1 || (filter && !filter.has(order[i].id))) continue;
              const dx = SX[i] - mouse[0], dy = SY[i] - mouse[1], d = dx * dx + dy * dy;
              if (d < bestD) { bestD = d; best = i; }
            }
            if (best !== hovered) {
              hovered = best;
              if (best >= 0) {
                const nd = order[best];
                tip.hidden = false;
                tip.innerHTML = `<b>${label(nd.id)}</b><br>HS ${nd.id} · ${sectorOf(nd.hs2)[1]}<br>PCI ${nd.pci.toFixed(2)} · world trade $${d3.format(".3s")(nd.trade * 1e3)}<br>${lit.has(nd.id) ? "<span class='copper'>● Indonesia exports competitively</span>" : "<span class='dim'>○ not yet an Indonesian strength</span>"}`;
              } else tip.hidden = true;
            }
            if (best >= 0) { tip.style.left = mouse[0] + 14 + "px"; tip.style.top = mouse[1] + 14 + "px"; }
          };
        }

        let running = true, tPrev = performance.now();
        const io = new IntersectionObserver(([en]) => { running = en.isIntersecting; }, { threshold: 0.05 });
        io.observe(canvas);
        function frame(t) {
          requestAnimationFrame(frame);
          const dt = Math.min((t - tPrev) / 1000, 0.1); tPrev = t;
          if (!running) return;
          if (auto) cam.yaw += autoSpeed * dt;
          if (!dragging && (Math.abs(vyaw) > 1e-4 || Math.abs(vpitch) > 1e-4)) {   // damping after release
            cam.yaw += vyaw; cam.pitch = Math.max(-1.35, Math.min(1.35, cam.pitch + vpitch)); vyaw *= 0.9; vpitch *= 0.9;
          }
          draw();
          if (interactive) resolveHover();
        }
        requestAnimationFrame(frame);

        return {
          setYear(yr) { lit = new Set(states[String(yr)] ?? []); },
          setFilter(ids) { filter = ids && ids.size ? ids : null; },
          setMode(m) { mode = m; layoutPositions(); },
          focus(id) {
            const i = indexOf.get(id); if (i == null) return;
